  "body": "For #60: a phone-triggered archive that preserves repository conversations, releases, and attachment bytes in a dedicated `repository-archive` branch.\n\nThe Python standard-library exporter paginates open and closed issues and PRs, discussion comments, reviews, inline review comments, PR commit comments, release notes/assets, tags, and generated release ZIP/TAR archives. Raw JSON and original source URLs are retained. Large media is split into parts of at most 40 MiB, with both part and whole-file SHA-256 verification; the archive includes an offline verification/restoration script.\n\nThe workflow runs tests, exports, verifies, and publishes using its automatic `GITHUB_TOKEN`. Publication uses a separate Git index and bounded upload batches, then advances the archive branch only after every file has arrived. No personal token, paid service, Git LFS, or Python package installation is needed. Failed API calls or real downloads keep the snapshot partial and prevent publication. Literal example paths such as `assets/xxxx` remain in the source text but are not treated as uploaded files.\n\nRun from a phone: **Actions → Archive repository → Run workflow**. In this demonstration the output goes to my fork; after merging, running the workflow here writes the archive directly into this repository. Full instructions: [docs/REPOSITORY_ARCHIVE.md](https://github.com/dziurawiecwempe582-hub/THE-ERROR-IS-THE-MESSAGE/blob/codex/repository-archive/docs/REPOSITORY_ARCHIVE.md).\n\nActual hosted demonstration against `attogram/THE-ERROR-IS-THE-MESSAGE`:\n\n- [Successful GitHub Actions run](https://github.com/dziurawiecwempe582-hub/THE-ERROR-IS-THE-MESSAGE/actions/runs/34750231467), including export, full-byte verification, and confirmed publication, completed in 5m27s.\n- [Published archive at immutable commit a544d98](https://github.com/dziurawiecwempe582-hub/THE-ERROR-IS-THE-MESSAGE/tree/a544d98b4f25be65014a87834b10e92fa9992661/archive): 60 issues, 6 PRs, 168 discussion comments, 4 releases, 4 tags, and 401 downloaded files totaling 1,895,824,852 bytes. This includes all 8 generated release source archives. The manifest is complete with zero failures.\n- Test 1, “consume this issue”: the published snapshot contains #60's text, its 11 comments at collection time, and all 53 distinct uploaded attachments referenced there. I read those published metadata files back from GitHub, checked their hashes against the manifest, and verified that no expected attachment URL was missing.\n- 35 tests pass locally on Windows. The hosted Linux run passes 34 and skips the one Windows-specific path test. The suite includes real local Git publication tests, pagination, missing/corrupt data, reconstruction, and safe redirects.\n\nThe implementation commit used for the hosted run is `84fac3827327caef80511c7b2ca53e341c025799`, which is the current PR head.\n\nThis is a time-bounded snapshot of accessible source material. It cannot recover deleted/inaccessible data or atomically freeze changes made while the API is being read. The archive branch stores ordinary Git objects, so frequent large media changes increase repository history.\n\nDisclosure: this implementation and its tests were developed and run by OpenAI Codex acting for @dziurawiecwempe582-hub; no independent human review is claimed. Please confirm acceptance for the stated €100 bounty and whether PayPal is available for payout. Any payment identifier will be supplied privately.\n\n<!-- repository-archive-refresh:34751725051 -->\nRepeat-run verification after new source material arrived:\n\n- [Successful refresh run 34751725051](https://github.com/dziurawiecwempe582-hub/THE-ERROR-IS-THE-MESSAGE/actions/runs/34751725051) reused the same implementation and updated the archive branch without changing the code branch.\n- [Immutable refreshed archive abb470a](https://github.com/dziurawiecwempe582-hub/THE-ERROR-IS-THE-MESSAGE/tree/abb470ae0c11276bc5f6f1ef7ba545283a107b26/archive): 60 issues, 10 PRs, 176 discussion comments, 1 review, 5 inline review comments, 4 releases, and 406 downloaded files (1,909,386,301 bytes), including all 8 generated release source archives. The manifest is complete with zero failures.\n- Issue #60 now has 18 archived comments and all 58 distinct attachments referenced in those records, including all 5 attachments in [the 10:22:24 UTC comment](https://github.com/attogram/THE-ERROR-IS-THE-MESSAGE/issues/60#issuecomment-5652685484). I independently read the immutable manifest and issue records back, checked their SHA-256 hashes and attachment coverage, and confirmed that every manifest file is present in the published Git tree with the expected size.\n\nThis snapshot began collection at 10:23:40 UTC. Comments added at 10:24 UTC or later, after that issue had been collected, belong to a subsequent snapshot; this repeat run demonstrates the refresh process without claiming an atomic view of a live repository.\n\n",
